==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|syndicat|lang=fr||office of [[syndic]], board of syndics, trade union}}, from {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|syndic|lang=fr||administrator}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|lang=la|syndicus}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|σύνδικος||caretaker of issue|lang=grc}}.

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun}}

# A [[group]] of individuals or companies formed to transact some specific [[business]], or to promote a common interest; a self-coordinating group.
# A similar group of [[gangster]]s engaged in [[organized crime]].
# A chain of [[newspaper]]s, or an agency that distributes features to multiple newspapers.
# The [[office]] or [[jurisdiction]] of a [[syndic]]; a [[council]] or body of syndics.
#: {{rfquotek|Bishop Burnet}}

====Synonyms====
* (roughly) &mdash; business partners

